  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Return and Reintegration Assistance to Trafficked Victims in Japan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will further strengthen the existing IOM voluntary return mechanism in Japan through continued facilitation of safe and humane return home for victims of trafficking (VoTs), within the objective of improving the protection and sustainable reintegration of VoTs and migration management of the Government of Japan. With provision of safe and dignified return and reintegration assistance to VoTs, the project&apos;s target outcomes are that identified VoTs in Japan who wish to return home are able to do so safely, voluntarily and with dignity and that beneficiaries are economically self-sufficient, psychosocially well, and socially integrated in their communities.</narrative>
  </description>
